---
import ContentPageLayout from '../../layouts/ContentPageLayout.astro';
import SectionHeader from '../../components/SectionHeader.astro';
import FeatureItem from '../../components/FeatureItem.astro';
---

<ContentPageLayout
  title="AI Readiness Assessment | Fighting Smart Cyber"
  description="Two-week structured audit of your business workflows, technology stack, and operations. Identify, prioritize, and quantify AI-driven automation opportunities with a flat-fee Phase 1 engagement."
  heroTitle='AI Readiness <span class="highlight">Assessment</span>'
  heroSubtitle="A two-week, flat-fee audit that maps your operations and prioritizes AI-driven automation"
  ctaTitle="Ready to Find Your AI Quick Wins?"
  ctaDescription="A $2,500 flat-fee Phase 1 engagement, fully credited toward any Phase 2 implementation within 180 days."
  ctaPrimaryButton={{ text: 'Start an Assessment', href: '/contact' }}
  ctaSecondaryButton={{ text: 'View All Solutions', href: '/solutions' }}
>
  <section class="bg-image-section overlay-left">
    <img src="/images/site/ai-readiness-bg.jpg" alt="" class="bg-image" loading="lazy" />
    <div class="bg-image-overlay"></div>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="bg-content">
        <h2>Where AI Actually Pays Off in Your Business</h2>
        <p>Most teams know AI can streamline their operations — they just don't know <em>where</em> it makes the biggest difference, <em>which</em> tools fit their stack, or <em>what</em> a realistic <abbr title="Return on Investment">ROI</abbr> looks like.</p>
        <p>Our AI Readiness Assessment answers those questions. We conduct a structured audit of your current business workflows, technology stack, and operational processes, then identify, prioritize, and quantify the highest-leverage automation opportunities across your project lifecycle.</p>
        <h3>What the Assessment Covers</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Kickoff Interview</strong> - Structured 90-minute session with your principals and operations lead to capture workflows, pain points, tools in use, project volume, and priorities</li>
          <li><strong>Technology Stack Audit</strong> - Read-only review of project management, communications, intake, document workflows, accounting, time tracking, and marketing systems</li>
          <li><strong>Workflow Mapping</strong> - End-to-end documentation of your project lifecycle, from intake through closeout, with tasks, owners, tools, and time estimates per phase</li>
          <li><strong>Automation Opportunity Analysis</strong> - Prioritized opportunity matrix scored on time savings, implementation complexity, ROI, and alignment with your priorities</li>
          <li><strong>Tool Recommendations</strong> - Specific AI tools, platforms, and integrations matched to your workflows, budget, and technical environment — with licensing cost estimates</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="content-text" style="max-width: 800px;">
        <h2>Built for Practical Outcomes</h2>
        <p>This is not a strategy deck. It is a working document that names the workflows worth automating, the tools that fit your stack, and the order in which to do it.</p>
        <p>We focus on <strong>quick wins</strong> you can implement within days of the assessment concluding, alongside a longer roadmap of higher-investment opportunities for Phase 2.</p>
        <h3>What You Walk Away With</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Written Assessment Report</strong> - Current-state workflow documentation, prioritized opportunity matrix, ROI estimates per workflow area, and tool recommendations with cost breakdowns</li>
          <li><strong>Findings Presentation</strong> - 60-minute working session with your leadership team to review findings, answer questions, and align on next steps</li>
          <li><strong>Phase 2 Roadmap</strong> - Recommended implementation sequencing, investment ranges, and projected outcomes per initiative</li>
          <li><strong>System Access Log</strong> - Full record of every system accessed, purpose, and date — for your records and internal audit</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader title="The Lifecycle We Map" description="We document your end-to-end project flow across six phases — finding where AI removes friction at every step." />
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <FeatureItem
          title="Client Inquiry & Intake"
          description="Lead capture, qualification, scheduling, and initial response — often the first place AI eliminates repetitive overhead."
        />
        <FeatureItem
          title="Proposal & Scope Development"
          description="Estimation, proposal drafting, and scope alignment — frequently a high-ROI target for AI-assisted document generation."
        />
        <FeatureItem
          title="Design & Documentation"
          description="Core delivery workflows where AI augments — not replaces — expert judgment, with the biggest opportunities in coordination and revision cycles."
        />
        <FeatureItem
          title="Permitting"
          description="Compliance tracking, submission packages, and review correspondence — workflows where AI shines at structured document handling."
        />
        <FeatureItem
          title="Construction Administration"
          description="<abbr title='Request for Information'>RFI</abbr> handling, submittals, change orders, site reports — repetitive, document-heavy, and ripe for automation."
        />
        <FeatureItem
          title="Closeout & Reporting"
          description="Project archives, final deliverables, and reporting — where AI accelerates knowledge capture for future projects."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader title="How We Prioritize Opportunities" description="Every opportunity we identify is scored on the same four dimensions, so you can make funding decisions with real data." />
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <FeatureItem
          title="Time Savings Potential"
          description="Hours per week or month recovered by automating a given workflow — calculated against your actual project volume."
        />
        <FeatureItem
          title="Implementation Complexity"
          description="Realistic effort to roll out, including integration, training, and process change. We flag what's a one-week lift versus a multi-month project."
        />
        <FeatureItem
          title="Estimated ROI"
          description="Projected return based on time saved, error reduction, and quality improvements — compared against tool licensing and implementation cost."
        />
        <FeatureItem
          title="Priority Alignment"
          description="How well the opportunity matches the strategic priorities you tell us about in kickoff — not just generic best practice."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section-alt">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader title="Engagement Details" description="A flat-fee, fixed-scope engagement designed to deliver value before you commit to a larger investment." />
      <div class="feature-grid">
        <FeatureItem
          title="Two-Week Delivery"
          description="Completed within approximately two weeks of signed SOW, NDA, and Data Handling Addendum — contingent on timely access and responsiveness."
        />
        <FeatureItem
          title="$2,500 Flat Fee"
          description="Fixed price, no hourly billing. No additional charges unless scope changes are agreed in writing in advance."
        />
        <FeatureItem
          title="Fully Credited to Phase 2"
          description="The entire $2,500 engagement fee is credited toward any Phase 2 implementation engagement contracted within 180 days."
        />
        <FeatureItem
          title="Strict Data Handling"
          description="Read-only or observer-level access where technically possible. NDA and Data Handling Addendum executed up front. No access to your clients' personal data beyond what's necessary to understand workflow structure."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="dark-section">
    <div class="container">
      <SectionHeader title="Why FSC for This Work" />
      <div class="content-grid">
        <div class="content-text">
          <p>We are operators who build, deploy, and run real systems — not consultants selling AI hype. That perspective shapes every recommendation we make:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>We've integrated AI into our own workflows</strong> and know what actually delivers value versus what looks impressive in a demo</li>
            <li><strong>We understand security and data handling</strong> — critical when you're evaluating AI tools that touch client data, proprietary work, or regulated workflows</li>
            <li><strong>We build custom software</strong> when off-the-shelf tools don't fit — so our recommendations are honest about where to buy, where to integrate, and where to build</li>
            <li><strong>We won't recommend a tool we wouldn't deploy ourselves</strong> — and we tell you when the right answer is "no AI here yet"</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="content-text">
          <p>The Assessment is intentionally scoped as a low-risk first engagement. You get a complete, written deliverable in two weeks for a flat fee, with no obligation to move into a larger Phase 2.</p>
          <p>If you do choose to move forward with implementation, the full assessment fee credits back — so you've effectively paid for diligence, not for a sales pitch.</p>
          <p>Ready to find your highest-leverage AI opportunities? Let's talk.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</ContentPageLayout>
